From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANYBOOK: amdgpu: allocate through Mesa's GBM, linear-only
 without it

Mesa 24.3 and later no longer export __driDriverGetExtensions_<driver>, so
dri.c cannot drive radeonsi any more and the amdgpu backend could not be
built (AOSP never listed dri.c in minigbm_core_files).

dri_gbm.c implements dri.h on Mesa's public GBM API instead:
- libgbm (libgbm_mesa.so on Android) is dlopen()ed RTLD_LOCAL; its GBM
  device sits on a separate render-node fd and is created on first use,
  so processes that only import buffers never load the gallium driver.
- Allocations go through gbm_bo_create() and reach minigbm's fd through
  PRIME; the GBM bo is dropped right away (the kernel BO keeps radeonsi's
  tiling metadata).
- Mapping a tiled buffer imports a GBM bo for that mapping only and lets
  the driver detile/retile.
- GBM has no modifier query, so tiled layouts are the driver's choice
  (TILE_TYPE_DRI).

amdgpu.c falls back to linear buffers when no DRI/GBM allocator is
available, or when debug.minigbm.amdgpu.linear_only=true (debug.* is
readable by every domain, so the mapper in app processes sees it too).

The generic libminigbm_gralloc gains the amdgpu backend. It only binds to
DRM devices named "amdgpu", so virtio-gpu and the other drivers are
unaffected.

Tested on Linux against Mesa 26.2 radeonsi on a Radeon 610M (RDNA2):
GPU-only buffers come out 64 KiB-tiled (swizzle mode 27); GPU-rendered
content reads back correctly through a mapping in a second driver
instance and vice versa; CPU buffers are linear. Test:
scripts/minigbm-amdgpu-host-test.sh in the AnyBook repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I75e95394dd2dba554de59ad414a80e5203db852d
---
 Android.bp |   8 +-
 amdgpu.c   |  11 +-
 dri_gbm.c  | 518 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 531 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dri_gbm.c

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 71e6c62..0f0a735 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ filegroup {
     srcs: [
